videos.script:
Today the planner leaves the phone and becomes a desktop app, with a window, a place on the computer, and files of its own. {{desktop}}

Electron does that by carrying a whole browser and a whole Node.js inside the app. {{two}} The browser shows the page. Node is the main process, and it can do anything the user can. Between them is one door, and you build it. {{door}}

First the window, which opens empty, and the reason is in an address. {{empty}} Then the fix, a site served from inside the app, as Capacitor did on the phone. {{served}}

Then the door. {{ipc}} The page asks the main process to write a file, and you will find that file on the disk. And the walls around the door: what a script in the page can reach, and what it cannot. {{walls}}

All of it runs on a computer with no screen, which is also how you test it in CI. {{xvfb}}
